---
/**
 * Main
 *
 * The dashboard's content panel: the `<main>` landmark the page's own content
 * is slotted into, and the target of both `ScrollToTop`'s `#top` anchor and the
 * skip link at the top of `Layout`.
 *
 * `tabindex="-1"` is there for that skip link: a fragment link pointing at an
 * element that cannot hold focus leaves focus behind in some browsers, so the
 * jump moves the viewport without moving the keyboard. It makes the landmark
 * focusable programmatically only, never by tabbing, and browsers reserve the
 * focus ring for `:focus-visible`, so nothing draws one.
 *
 * It carries no styling of its own. `.main` places it in the shell's grid and
 * gives it the content inset, `.dash-surface` paints it; both live in
 * `global.css` beside the other panels (see "Panel surfaces" there).
 *
 * @component
 *
 * @slot default - The page's content.
 */

interface Props {}
---

<main id="top" class="main dash-surface" tabindex="-1">
    <slot/>
</main>
